vec3 position = _vert_position + translation;
// Test: does Sodium's per-region clock show at region borders? Sodium has no GameTime; u_CurrentTime is the
// milliseconds since the region (8 x 4 x 8 sections) was created. As a clock that wraps every 1200 s, with a
// whole number of cycles per wrap (200: a 6 s period). The position inside the region (its origin is on the
// world grid, every 128 blocks in x and z), with a 16-block wavelength, which divides 128: the wave is
// continuous across region borders in space, so a step there can only come from the clock.
vec3 inRegion = _vert_position + _get_draw_translation(_draw_id);
float clock = float(u_CurrentTime % 1200000) / 1200000.0;
position.y += 1.2 * sin(6.2831853 * (inRegion.x / 16.0 + clock * 200.0)) * cos(6.2831853 * inRegion.z / 16.0);
